{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>You</b> — It is possible that it is a form of צר like 'enemy,' or the constriction of illness, like צר ומצוק, and the proof is 'the multitudes of pains' [Psalalm 32:6]." "<b>Shout for deliverance</b> — Rabbi Moses said: the verb will govern two objects, the voices of angels: 'I will deliver,' and then 'shout,' in the manner of 'and the shout passed,' and they will testify against me and say 'I will instruct you'; in this way you go, like זאת and it lacks a bet from עיני. And some say: it is in the sense of רמז."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "The argument is compressed and textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The bet lacking from עיני may allude to a proposed emendation to בעיני ('in my eyes') or similar; the reference is obscure."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:14.721988873Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}